abstract: >-
  Agentic coding benchmarks grade artifacts from single execution traces.
  Many requirements on agent-authored control systems are hyperproperties
  (predicates over sets of traces). DIPTYCH is a paired-trace grading harness
  with eight perturbation operators, coupling discipline, and a probe-tree
  cost model. A mutation sweep found and fixed three classes of defect in its
  own graders, and in a pilot with 20 model-written controllers, 12 of the 15
  that pass every single-trace check violate a requirement under paired
  probing. No accuracy, AUROC, or model rankings are claimed.
